  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-mcp-overview",
      "text": "Read-only MCP server overview for the DeepSeek Harness web GUI. Adds an \"MCP Servers\" section under Settings that shows each configured `dsh-mcp-client` server with its connection status, transport, endpoint/command, and the `mcp__*` tools it registers — without touching any server or writing state."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Prerequisites: a DeepSeek Harness install with the `dsh` CLI and the web profile.\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-mcp-overview\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "What you see",
      "text": "Open Settings → **MCP Servers**. For every server entry mounted by `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` (the servers you configure in your profile's `cordis.patch.yml`), the section lists:\n\n- **server name** — the `serverName` from the entry's config;\n- **transport** — `stdio`, `streamable-http`, or `unknown` when the config cannot be read;\n- **endpoint or command** — the URL or the launch command;\n- **registered tools** — every `mcp__<server>__<tool>` schema the server exposes (public-name sorted)."
    },
    {
      "section": "What you see",
      "text": "The list is read-only: it assembles a snapshot from the Loader and the tool registry and never edits configuration or calls into the MCP servers."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compression",
      "text": "MCP tool descriptions and JSON Schemas can be verbose in a model context. `dsh-mcp-overview` narrows tool payloads through the `system-prompt/assemble` pipeline according to the profile's `toolCompression` setting:\n\n- `brief` (default) — keep the first sentence of each description; drop `examples`, `default`, `title`, and other documentation-only JSON-Schema keys.\n- `names` — keep only names and parameter name/type pairs (most aggressive).\n- `none` — no trimming."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- Harness release on the `0.1.2-alpha.1` service vocabulary or newer\n- The `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` bundle (ships with the harness base) plus at least one configured MCP server in the profile"
    },
    {
      "section": "Model Experience",
      "text": "The overview is a settings panel, not an agent tool: no model-visible tool or command is added, so agent behavior is unchanged."
    }
  ],
  "skipped": []
